2026-06-10 13:03:53 | INFO | LLM response | purpose=chat_response | duration_min=0.0088 | response_chars=479 | content=Sure! To make idli, start by soaking idli rice and urad dal separately for 4–6 hours. Grind them into smooth batters, then mix them in a 3:1 ratio (rice to dal). Let the batter ferment overnight in a warm place. The next day, add salt and a bit of curd to the batter and mix well. Pour the batter into greased idli cups and steam them for about 10–12 minutes. Once done, let them sit for a few minutes before gently removing them from the cups. Serve hot with chutney and sambar.
